WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.992
Emperor Xiaowen of the Northern Wei was still young, yet he already had a bold idea.

00:00:05.342 --> 00:00:08.582
He hoped his country would grow stronger and his people would live better lives.

00:00:08.932 --> 00:00:15.580
He wanted to move the capital from Pingcheng to Luoyang, but many Xianbei ministers opposed the idea.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:19.962
The ministers discussed it heatedly; some shook their heads and sighed.

00:00:20.312 --> 00:00:26.144
Emperor Xiaowen thought of a clever plan: he pretended to lead a southern expedition, and so the great army set out.

00:00:26.494 --> 00:00:31.054
The wind and rain along the way were heavy, yet the column marched on.

00:00:31.404 --> 00:00:37.308
When they reached Luoyang, he suddenly announced: From today on, this is the new capital!

00:00:37.658 --> 00:00:41.690
The ministers looked at one another, and had no choice but to accept the decision.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.600
New palaces were built, and the city of Luoyang grew livelier and livelier.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:51.630
Merchants, scholars, and craftsmen all came to settle in Luoyang.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:01:00.812
Luoyang later became the political and cultural center of the Northern Wei, and Emperor Xiaowen's decision changed history.

